  {
    "sha": "fa62d89b89d8a8a3ba07022a9accdcc43b270c74",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGZhNjJkODliODlkOGE4YTNiYTA3MDIyYTlhY2NkY2M0M2IyNzBjNzQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T14:10:36Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-24T14:10:36Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): the Tools ribbon cell opens a tool library window\n\nThe tool library leaves the dock for its own non-modal window\n(id tool-library), which can stay open beside the viewport while\nProperties keeps its subject. The four doors (ribbon Tools cell, View\nmenu, the gate route for no tool and for no fitting tool) open it\nthrough actions::target with the empty tool name.\n\nThe window lists the Document tools (T, Tool, Kind, diameter, flute\nlength, flutes, holder, recipes) and the Catalog tools, with the Tool\ntype and Name filters and the New, Export and Import buttons of the\nold tab. Add is still AddTool and Import is still ImportTools.\n\nLayoutRequest::ToolLibrary goes. Tab::Tools stays for serde, and a\nsaved panel setup that holds it still loads: decode drops the tab.\n\nFixes #3892\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
